    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 1111b8402080cea8b0da54dcc268dfcce42d014a -->\n\nReview by SlaveSession. Built locally in a reviewer worktree. The trial merge with main is clean.\n\nGate result: camcraft-app lib 388 passed, 0 failed. All six step-suite binaries pass. Clippy is clean.\n\nWhat the change does:\n- `fit()` returns a reason with a name. Seven reasons exist.\n- `judged()` logs the face, and returns facets kept with off = UNMEASURED.\n- UNMEASURED is 1000 file units. It passes every verdict tolerance, in millimetres and in inches. It stays under the UNKNOWN_MM sentinel.\n- `verify` refuses a model that holds UNMEASURED. A face the kernel cannot measure never passes as full fidelity. This obeys the Prime Directive.\n\nNotes:\n- Planes keep the silent KEPT path. Correct: a plane always measures.\n- The unit-sweep test pins the sentinel guard for k in 1e-3, 1, 25.4, 1e6.\n- The body says the user-facing message stays generic (TOO_COARSE). Follow-up #2733 (P7) tracks the clearer text. The decision file matches the code.\n\nVerdict: merge-ready. This is a P3 fix, not P1 floor work, so no second review is needed.\n",
